  "question": "A physical quantity $P$ is related to four observations $a$, $b$, $c$ and $d$ as follows:\n\n$$P = a^3b^2/c\\sqrt{d}$$\n\nThe percentage errors of measurement in $a$, $b$, $c$ and $d$ are $1\\%$, $3\\%$, $2\\%$, and $4\\%$ respectively. The percentage error in the quantity $P$ is",
  "diagram": "",
  "diagram_alt": "",
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$10\\%$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$2\\%$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$13\\%$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$15\\%$",
      "image": ""
    }
  ],
  "answer": "C",
  "numerical_answer": "",
  "tolerance": "",
  "solution": "$$\\frac{\\Delta P}{P} = 3\\frac{\\Delta a}{a} + 2\\frac{\\Delta b}{b} + \\frac{\\Delta c}{c} + \\frac{1}{2}\\frac{\\Delta d}{d}$$\n\n$$= 3(1\\%) + 2(3\\%) + 2\\% + \\frac{1}{2}(4\\%) = 3 + 6 + 2 + 2 = 13\\%$$",
